Anti-Dowry Awareness Campaign at Borbila Village\nOne Day Workshop on Performance of Bihu and Folk Instruments, organised by Departments of English, A\nProfile\nFaculty Members\nActivities\nAchievements\nQuestion Paper\nSyllabus\nPO & CO\nNewsletter\nProfile\nThe Department of Arabic was established in 2004 as part of the institution’s expansion into diverse language studies. It aims to promote linguistic proficiency and cultural understanding of the Arabic language. The introduction of Major courses in 2011 marked a significant development. The department focuses on both classical and modern Arabic studies. In alignment with NEP 2020, it emphasizes skill-based and interdisciplinary learning. The curriculum includes language, literature, and cultural studies. Students are encouraged to develop communication and translation skills. The department promotes cultural exchange and global perspectives. Faculty members provide academic guidance and mentoring. The teaching-learning process includes discussions and project work. It also emphasizes research and language proficiency. The department contributes to enhancing students’ academic and career prospects.\nFaculty Members\nGAZIBAR RAHMAN\nASSISTANT PROFESSOR\ngazibarrahman1995@gmail.com\nM.A\nBAHADUR ALI AHMED\nASSISTANT PROFESSOR CUM HOD\nbahaduraliahmed901@gmail.com\nM.A., NET\nABDUL KHALEQUE\nASSISTANT PROFESSOR\nM.A., M.PHIL., B.ED\nActivities\nActivity\nDescription\nDate\nView\nDoor-to-Door Anti-Dowry Awareness Campaign at Borbila Village\nThe NSS Unit, Departments of Arabic, Economics and Political Science of Manikpur Anchalik College, i\n2026-05-30\nView File\nOne-Day Workshop on Performance of Bihu and Folk Instruments, organised by Departments of English, Assamese, Arabic, and Sanskrit\nA One-Day Workshop on Performance of Bihu and Folk Instruments has been organised by the Departments\n2026-03-18\nView File\nAchievements\nAchievement\nDate\nView\nQuestion Papers\nPrint\nSemester\nYear\nView\nQR Code\nBA I\nVi